nd of like i i  don't have one of those and they're  pretty expensive at the time i thought  they were prohibitively expensive and  it's just a fraction of where they are  today he was just like well if you want  to you know stay on this call whatever  like we're going to go out and buy and  so he kind of forced us all to go out  there and buy punk and this was the punk  that i bought it opened up my eyes to  just like what the marketplace could  provide in terms of collector culture in  terms of the psychology around nfts and  understanding the trading and the  experience of it all this is important  for me i don't think i'll ever get rid  of it there have been a few moments in  the marketplace where i could have  unloaded it and done pretty well  but  again there's a sentimentality around  the crypto punks and especially this one  because without this i don't think i  would have understood the mechanics  around our own project and so this was a  very expensive piece of education for me  how much was it how much is it worth now  oh well was it what was the best offer  you got  it was at the time it was  twenty thousand dollars u.s when punks  were peaking at some point in  the later half of the year there were  probably it was probably  about a half million dollars  which happens with nfts  it's somewhere in between there at this  point um  [Music]  but yeah  crazy

